      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In your .asset file you can find a base64 string that when decoded to text reveals a json object that contains program byte code, heap, heap default values and symbol tables. \nI guess it can be a bit confusing as the program heap is created internally and has no indicator on the Udon Behavior UI except for public variables. This is probably because there are no instructions for passing values to variables directly in Udon Assembly, but only from 1 heap object to another.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
